   "source": [
    "# SEP4 — Kamtjatka Fire Monitoring: Data Preparation\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook does three things:\n",
    "1. **Parses the IoT team's MQTT log files** → exports a clean labeled `iot_data.xlsx`\n",
    "2. **Loads the Blattmann smoke detection dataset** → exports the raw version as `blattmann_raw.xlsx`\n",
    "3. **Processes Blattmann** → drops features the ENS160 device does not produce, renames columns to match IoT naming, and exports `blattmann_processed.xlsx`\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### Before running\n",
    "Download the Blattmann dataset from Kaggle:\n",
    "- URL: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/deepcontractor/smoke-detection-dataset\n",
    "- Download the CSV file and place it in this folder as: `smoke_detection_iot.csv`\n",
    "\n",
    "Everything else runs automatically.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### Class labels used across both datasets\n",
    "| Class ID | Label | Description |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| 0 | No Smoke | Normal ambient air — no event |\n",
    "| 1 | Smoke | Active cooking smoke / fire event |\n",
    "| 2 | Steam | High-humidity false alarm (shower, kettle, steam) |"
   ]
  },
